\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Tate's postban monologue, \u8220 Andrew Tate Final Message,\u8221  was reposted in its entirety from Tate's original account, TateSpeech (now unavailable), by a YouTube user called The Tate Bible on August 23, 2022. The video was screen-recorded and archived for analysis on August 24, 2022, along with the 2,848 available comments on the YouTube video. In the hour-long video, Tate discusses the social media ban and other topics he wanted to address before stepping away from his platform; in the comments, viewers\u8212 mostly Tate supporters\u8212 share their perspective (s) on the ban, perceived impacts of Tate's content on their lives, and more. The video and comments were analyzed separately. For analysis, the video was distributed among four independent coders. A sample of comments (}
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 n\u8201 }{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2 =\u8201 300) was divided evenly and distributed to five independent coders.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24
\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Thematic Analysis}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260
\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The research team performed a thematic analysis following Braun and Clarke's (2012) system of doing a close reading of the data (video or comments), assigning codes, coming together to compare, consolidating codes into themes, and describing each theme and its implications for the research questions. This was done in two rounds for both the video and the comments to ensure that the themes were as solid as possible. The following results reflect the analyses. To retain the integrity of user comments, no grammatical or syntactical corrections were made to quotes unless absolutely necessary for clarity.}
