\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Results}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Themes in Andrew Tate's Final Message Video}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{
\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The \u8220 hardship builds character\u8221  argument}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha
\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Tate opens the video by discussing his life, which he describes as having \u8220 always been difficult\u8221  (00:00:31). He emphasizes that he is happy about the difficulties he encountered because \u8220 as a man, trauma and difficulty is extremely important because it's the building blocks for mental fortitude and physical fortitude\u8221  (00:00:38). He then goes on to recount stories of times he had to overcome adversity in his youth because of bullying. The core message of those stories is summed up by what Tate's father allegedly said to him when he was 5 years old after Tate confided to his father that two older boys were bullying him on the bus, which was, \u8220 son, if you want to deal with this, you're going to have to deal with it yourself\u8221  (00:02:04).}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Tate's discussion of his life story and the difficulties he faced during his developmental years illuminates a socialization process, spearheaded by his father, where he was made to feel that it was his responsibility as a man to deal with any difficulties he faced on his own. According to Tate, this process of facing life's challenges on his own led to his development of an \u8220 iron mind\u8221  (00:06:27), which allows him to be emotionally unaffected by things that happen to him. Instead of working to understand the importance of emotional intelligence and empathy, Tate asks his followers to \u8220 man up\u8221  and power through any challenges they may face, emphasizing his hypermasculine \u8220 War Room\u8221  approach to problem-solving and reinforcing symptoms of his facilitation of male collective narcissism.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Further, Tate's narration of his life story helps to create norms for his followers and also establish himself as a prototypical leader. By creating these group norms centered around callous-unemotionality, he provides his followers with a specific type of masculinity to identify with, and he sets the stage for excluding those who do not adhere to or respect that specific version of masculinity (see Reicher et al., 2008). By using his own life to create these group norms, he is able to establish himself as a prototypical leader. Prototypical leaders are viewed as \u8220 competent enough to guide [followers] towards positive outcomes\u8221  and \u8220 so honest and benevolent towards [followers] that they will put the group's interests ahead of their personal ones\u8221  (Milesi, 2022, p. 887). This (errantly) assumed benevolence may lead group members to support toxic environments such as this one (Milesi, 2022).}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The ban as a barrier between Tate and the \u8220 public consciousness\u8221 }{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260
\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 It is his \u8220 iron mind,\u8221  Tate argues, that has blocked out the \u8220 narratives [that] have managed to gain such a foothold in popular consciousness\u8221  (0:06:16), leaving him unmotivated to address them earlier because they did not affect him personally and/or emotionally. Tate admits that he made a mistake allowing the narrative that he is problematic to go unchallenged because \u8220 the public consciousness has been polluted to a point where narratives are being purported which are absolutely and utterly false\u8221  (00:07:17). He then doubles down on his claim that he is addressing the situation now }
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 not}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2  because he is personally emotionally affected by the ban or the commentary leading up to and surrounding the ban, but because the situation is \u8220 having a genuine negative impact on the people who [he] care[s] about and the people who care about [him] \u8230  despite the fact it doesn't emotionally affect [him], as a man [he has] a duty to protect all of those [he] love[s] \u8230  and for this reason, these narratives have started to become very, very harmful\u8221  (00:07:28). There is an interesting conflict between the narratives \u8220 hurting\u8221  those he loves and he himself reportedly feeling no hurt or negative emotions, once again positioning him as \u8220 above\u8221  others who may be \u8220 weak enough\u8221  to experience emotion through social comparison.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Tate continues to assert that the attacks against him are driven by malice and that he did not address them because he felt it would be pointless since those attacking him already hate him and will continue to lie no matter what. He claims that he was not mad at Instagram for banning him because he understood why they felt the need to do it, but he notes that \u8220 [he] believe[s] it's not the right thing to do because it doesn't allow [him] to shift the public consciousness in a constructive manner\u8221  (00:35:23). It is unclear why he feels that it is his personal responsibility to \u8220 shift the public consciousness,\u8221  but he is disappointed that he has been prevented from doing so and refuses to let on that it has had such a strong effect on him.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I pray for my haters}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24
\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Throughout the video, Tate makes frequent religious references to himself and to the social media ban as a part of his divine destiny. Tate explains that everything he has advocated for in his content and the timeline of events that have occurred throughout his career are all a part of his life as a religious man. He implies that God could reverse the ban, saying \u8220 if God wants me to have an Instagram, then I will\u8221  (00:36:21), and comparing the ban to a plot point in scripture\u8212 \u8220 the Bible is full of redemption stories\u8221  (01:02:05)\u8212 that it is a \u8220 life path change that God has chosen for [him]\u8221  (01:02:20). Tate's religious references provide an interesting point of contrast in that he begins the video telling a story about a time that he beat up a classmate with a lunchbox, repeatedly references how he has been wronged in the past instead of turning the other cheek, explicitly states that he is \u8220 not an emotional person [and] do[es] not do emotional responses\u8221  (00:35:10), continues to assert that he has \u8220 done nothing wrong\u8201 \u8230 \u8201 [and] God know[s] what [his] innocence is\u8221  (00:07:09), and many more points of irony. Importantly, Tate's male collective narcissism allows for self-positioning as faultless and incapable of doing wrong, meaning neither he nor his followers must feel responsible for the harm they do to other people, and women in particular.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Tate's references to himself as someone who is a leader and source of inspiration for his followers are often religious in nature as well; examples include reframing his ban as a willing sacrifice in which he has had to \u8220 martyr [his] presence on social media to raise a conversation which is going to be a net benefit for the world as a whole\u8221  (00:37:51), and that it is his \u8220 cross to bear because of [his] monumental success\u8221  (00:52:24). Tate even implies that he \u8220 has helped [his followers\u8217 ] mind[s and] cured their depression\u8221  (00:18:56), a feat of healing that he attributes to the content of his HU classes. Based on Tate's previous appearances with Alex Jones, Paul Joseph Watson, and Donald Trump Jr. (Das, 2022b), as well as his open critiques of \u8220 liberals\u8221  in the final message video, it is not a major assumption to place Tate on the conservative end of the political spectrum where these religious references would serve him in his efforts to reach a staunch right-wing audience.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Surprisingly, following the Tate brothers\u8217  indictment and subsequent release, Andrew claimed to have converted to Islam, creating a paradoxical alignment with the conservative right and, simultaneously, Muslim ideals (Ali, 2023; Samir, 2022). In an interview with fellow controversial figure and British rapper, Nzube Olisaebuka Udezue (better known as \u8220 Zuby\u8221 ), Tate addressed the confusion surrounding his conversion to Islam, claiming that it was a simple decision, since he no longer wanted to identify as Christian; he explained, \u8220 There is one religion on the planet today in which people stand up for the rules \u8230  they refuse to be mocked, and they refuse to completely throw away their values and belief system under the guise of \u8216 tolerance\u8217  cause they don\u8217 t want to be tolerant of everything \u8230  and that's Islam\u8221  (Udezue, 2022, 05:33). It remains unclear whether Tristan also converted. The public and the Muslim community have reported mixed reactions to Tate's conversion to the religion. Some Muslims view it positively since his conversion has inspired some fans to embrace the religion themselves, while others argue that his conversion is a veiled strategy spurring Muslim people who already follow him to do the footwork of defending his messages, and to better his business practices in Dubai (Feltham & Simpson, 2024).}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 \u8220 The world is built on the backs of strong men\u8221 : personal and male collective narcissism}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0
\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Individuals with clinical narcissism\u8212 a personality }{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24
\ltrch\b\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf2 disorder}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 \u8212 feel that they are larger than life, superior to others, and entitled to special treatment and attention; true narcissists are often deeply jealous, apathetic about others\u8217  concerns and needs, and unbothered by how their actions impact those around them (Mayo Clinic Staff, n.d.). Importantly, clinical narcissism represents a pathology, and not every individual who exhibits narcissistic traits is a clinical narcissist. That is, an individual may exhibit relatively high levels of narcissism while being technically subclinical. Like clinical narcissism, subclinical narcissism is marked by grandiosity (Jones & Paulhus, 2014). For subclinical narcissists, their behavior is driven by a desperate need for ego-reinforcement and this drive can lead them toward self-destructive behaviors (Jones & Paulhus, 2014). Importantly, subclinical narcissists believe in their own self-promotion (Paulhus et al., 2018). They operate under the assumption that others admire them and when that belief is threatened, they become more likely to aggress (Paulhus et al., 2018).}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 While it is beyond the scope of this study to establish whether Andrew Tate is a clinical or subclinical narcissist, Andrew Tate exhibits many narcissistic traits in his content and managed to do so throughout his final message video as well. Examples include his frequent references to his \u8220 enormous wealth\u8221  (00:40:00), \u8220 monumental success\u8221  (00:52:03), and being \u8220 the most famous man on the planet\u8221  (00:41:40). Additionally, Tate likes to refer to himself with nicknames such as \u8220 Top G\u8221  (meaning \u8220 top gangster\u8221 ) and \u8220 Cobra Tate,\u8221  and cannot accept that he may be at fault for the fallout caused by his messages (e.g., \u8220 I\u8217 m genuinely not the bad person,\u8221  00:52:00). Tate also rationalizes attacks on his character as the result of jealousy and complains that the media has failed to recognize that he \u8220 run[s] a shelter for dogs in Romania \u8230  [and] rebuilt an entire orphanage \u8230  [and] didn\u8217 t use it for positive PR\u8221  (00:51:13), even though he seems to be doing exactly that in his video. Further, he tried to stir up more \u8220 positive PR\u8221  by making frequent reference to the Tate Foundation, which he alleged would \u8220 spend millions of dollars on philanthropy\u8221  (00:49:20). Thus far, there is no evidence that the Tate Foundation has donated any money or been concretely established at all.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Tate's narcissism is also especially well-demonstrated by his response to sexual assault and sex trafficking allegations made against him. When public attention surrounding Tate and the impending ban on his content reached its peak, conversations about previous sexual assault and sex trafficking allegations against him began to resurface. In such incidents, he allegedly \u8220 accidentally hit [a] woman [in a bar fight] and broke her jaw\u8221  (Das, 2022b, para. 17), had a police raid performed on his home based on a report that a woman was being held there and abused against her will\u8212 which Tate later denied, along with all other allegations that mistreated women to varying degrees\u8212 and acted as the aggressor in a variety of other ways (Das, 2022b). The Tate brothers have continued to move in and out of jail as trials against them for human trafficking and rape charges move through the Romanian justice system (Associated Press, 2023). In the video, Tate addresses the sex trafficking allegations against him not by arguing that he is }
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 not}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2  a rapist, nor by explicitly stating that rape is wrong, but instead by taking the stance that such claims are racist toward Romanians because they imply that \u8220 Romania is the kind of place that rape is okay\u8221  (00:53:01). By redirecting the focus of the allegations to sources external to himself, Tate reinforces his narcissism while refusing to take responsibility for the allegations mere minutes after calling himself a \u8220 man of [his] word\u8221  (00:43:54) and \u8220 a personal responsibility kind of person\u8221  (00:52:15). Though he spends quite a bit of time trying to communicate that he is a \u8220 good person,\u8221  it is less about condemning the actions he was accused of and more about referencing good deeds he }
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 has}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2  done and protecting his image. By protecting this image he believes he portrays, Tate can also maintain followers who use that image to justify their support and enact male collective narcissism, which could be reinforcing, in turn, a hegemonic masculinity based on incel and/or Tate-specific teachings.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Themes in the Comments on Andrew Tate's Final Message Video}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24
\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Andrew Tate as a messenger of truth, family member, and religious figure}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Comments in response to Tate's final message revealed not only the structure and demographics of his audiences but the specific facets of Tate's role as a media figure with a relationship to his followers and their reaction to his social media ban.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Tate as a Figure of \u8220 Truth\u8221 }{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24
\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The construction of Tate as a figure or \u8220 truth\u8221  is unsurprising given Tate's propensity toward delivering aspirational and religious messages, though the understanding of truth among commenters seems to vary. For some, truth is perceived as those messages that are typically silenced or not accepted by society: From a female perspective, you are very empowering. you are so intelligent, you have shifted my mind in to one of its greatest mindsets. thank you for being real, you are real and for that, you are being silenced. it's sad and proves a lot about society. i have waited for someone like you to come on the internet for so long. no one likes the truth anymore, we love you for being truthful. thank you for caring and showing how much you care for everyone and anyone. thank you for giving opportunities and showing how to be successful but happy. no one else does this, especially the way you do. thank you tate. [heart emoji] everyone in this world, needs you.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 For many, \u8220 truth\u8221  referred to the standardization of certain sociocultural systems (i.e., maintaining hypermasculinity, heteronormativity), systems that are allegedly under attack by the political left, the government, and the matrix (Dahir, 2022): This is a Real War. Truth, Masculinity, and Bravery is under attack. The Establishment has weaponized the Modern Women to crush Real Men because they are terrified that History will repeat itself. Our Founding Fathers were the Men that fought against the Evils of the Ruling Class.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 This comment mirrors Tate's rhetoric and messages promoted in online incel and male supremacist forums; such messages typically frame the out-group (s)\u8212 liberal people, feminists, women, and anyone else who has not \u8220 woken up\u8221  to the purported false reality of the matrix\u8212 as a threat to the in-group (Reicher et al., 2008), and in this case, truth itself. This rhetoric has the potential to undermine societal structures and dangerously urges Tate's followers to question their very realities. Commenters made sense of the matrix and concepts of reality, stating: There's thousands of reasons to hate someone and thousands more not to trust anyone. TATE YOUR TRACTION OF REALITY IS TRUE (REALIST) but the world can't handle the way you speak about it. if all of our minds would think alike, this world would be underpopulated SADLY. Woman don't understand the roll of a man, but you explained it 110% right.. wish you the best brotha!}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 This comment positions the world as operating under a matrix-like simulation that only Tate knows how to break free from. Other comments specifically named the matrix, such as \u8220 Fuck the matrix, im a fan no matter what, I\u8217 ll be rich in the next two years and we\u8217 re gonna meet up\u8221  and: If there are phrases like \u8216 The Last Man Standing against the poised Matrix\u8217 , \u8216 King of the New Age\u8217 , \u8216 The Conquerer\u8217 [\u8230 ] etc to be defined, the only answer are the Tate Brothers.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 What is particularly interesting to think about regarding \u8220 cancelation\u8221  and the matrix is that Tate maintained (prior to this video) that he operates outside of the matrix, and by doing so, cancelation is impossible. For instance, one commenter asked, \u8220 but i thought you didn\u8217 t care about being canceled? I thought you weren\u8217 t in the matrix? That's cute don\u8217 t be shy.\u8221  Another responded, \u8220 the top g got cancelled and hes crying about it now.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Tate as a \u8220 Savior\u8221 }{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24
\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 A key component to Tate's strategy, and where he shies away from traditional nodes of populism, is his supposed intent to help \u8220 losers\u8221  achieve wealth and success (i.e., creating the ultimate elite class), versus being a leader for the \u8220 common man\u8221  whom he respects. For instance, he previously told his fans, \u8220 Most of you are happy to be losers part time \u8230  You want to escape. That's why you joined [HU]. You don\u8217 t want to be a loser anymore\u8221  (Dahir, 2022, para. 2). This same sentiment was evident in the comments, with many thanking Tate for helping them overcome life obstacles and offering personal testimonies in which Tate has healed or fixed them in some way. Many commenters credit Tate with helping them achieve their fitness goals and weight loss, reaffirming their perceptions of gender, masculinity, and dating, improving their finances, and bettering their mental and emotional health. For example, one commenter explained, \u8220 I\u8217 ve been overweight my whole life and he's motivated me to quit complaining and work hard\u8230 i\u8217 m a female too and agree with most everything he says.\u8221  Another lauds Tate, saying: Ever since I came across your words and messages, I've started hitting the gym harder than last time. My primary focus has since been on broadening my network and bettering my financial circumstance, staying away from romantic relationships and channeling my energy towards developing the set of skills I have already amassed. That is what I try to instill in my friends as well. My father has noticed this as well. You have played a significant role in a time when I believe positive masculine presence is needed the most. Your impact will surely last for generations to come. God bless you. Sincerely.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 It is important to recognize that many of these messages have inherent problematic messaging, specifically displaying overt and covert sexism, misogyny, and skewed understandings of masculinity/femininity, as demonstrated by this comment: Honest to god\u8230  Andrew makes fucking sense of the situation in the world where every attractive woman I\u8217 ve dated lately also has been a \u8216 gold digger.\u8217  \u8230  My former understanding of it was that I kept meeting awful, psychopathic women. But honestly, and this is simply a statement of fact \u8212  this is how women are. If you\u8217 re a super hot girl, it's super hard to not also be entitled and expect things from men. I probably would be too, if I were a super hot young woman. Especially in today's culture. The man speaks truth. I have a lot more empathy for these women because of this. He also describes our duty as men, which fully relates to this. If I were a little bitch I would keep complaining and shaming women for being who they are. But no, it's just the way we are as people and as a man it's my duty to accommodate this \u8230 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Other commenters shared frustration with the way men are treated in society, expressing a decline in their perceptions of a pervasive societal worship of hegemonic masculinities:   In the last 10\u8201 +\u8201 years, masculinity has become frowned upon and whenever a man tries to speak the truth on social media, he tends to be muzzled and on real life castrated by the surrounding social construct \u8230  you are not allowed to disagree and prove different points of view anylonger \u8230 Men can\u8217 t have the role model we need and want cause women and tail riding men want to take it down cause they want to rule the world when we should really it belongs to on one\u8230 .\u8201 Andrew I had fun while it lasted thanks man Many commenters felt that systems of the matrix, namely politically left-leaning media, were responsible for the takedown and cancelation of Tate, and as a consequence, society is likely to become emasculated, lazy, poor, and even more adherent to the matrix. In line with Reicher et al.'s (2008) model of collective hate, these comments suggest that Tate's followers have identified the media as a threatening out-group that fails to adhere to the virtues of masculinity and, as such, they must fight back against the media to protect Tate and, by extension, the group. Such comments included: \u8220 We cant let these weak ass men running the social platforms win\u8221  and \u8220 in the land of the blind, the one eyed man is banned on all media outlets\u8230 \u8201 smh.\u8221  Others incorporated religious themes while pointing a finger at media: The truth will always prevail, The Tates have delivered the message its our time to take action. Stay strong and stay true do not give into this evil the media gives. God bless you all and keep your heads up.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Not only does this commenter allude to Tate brothers as prophetic savior figures, but they also encourage other commenters to join the fight against media censorship.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Tate as a Familial and Religious Figure}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Tate is often painted as a familial/kin presence in many commenters\u8217  lives. For example, one commenter remarks that \u8220 Tate taught us young men how we should live life the right way, teaching the truth, like a father, salute to you brother,\u8221  and another describes him as \u8220 the father we all needed.\u8221  In response to Tate's references to religion and being a \u8220 man of God\u8221  in his final message video, some commenters seemed to wrestle with his role as a religious figure, messiah, or martyr: All they can say is how he isn't shit or that he's hurting people \u8230  but notice that none of them have anything of value to say or teach. They stay safe and try not to offend anyone. And because of that, they can never stand up for the truth, because the truth is offensive in a world full of Liars\u8201 \u8230 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Yet, most of his followers seemed to accept his role as a religious figure, with many comparing him to Jesus, stating: \u8220 Top G died for us. Like Jesus. Top Gesus,\u8221  and citing biblical scriptures: \u8220 Proverbs 12:6-The words of the wicked are murderous, but the words of the righteous rescue those who are threatened.\u8221  In these comments, it is apparent that Tate was appointed as a messenger of \u8220 truth,\u8221  and those preventing any sort of message deliverance are defying God or part of a greater test of faith. For example, one commenter posted, \u8220 God tests his strongest soldiers. He wouldn\u8217 t give you something you couldn\u8217 t handle. He's the only one who can handle this all so eloquently.\u8221  Another commenter said: Please don't let this be your last message. You got so much more work to do. Your doing the Lords work and the devils are squealing. So don't let this destroy your message. We all love you. TOP fukn G.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Not only are the effects of Tate's male collective narcissism on his followers in this area rather shocking, but they are reminiscent of those incurred by cult leaders such as David Koresh who have claimed to be the reincarnation of Jesus Christ; by leaning on the \u8220 cult of personality,\u8221  Tate manages to assert that he \u8220 exists on a separate plane from ordinary people\u8221  (Koch, 2022, p. 198) and can somehow draw his followers into that plane. Such rhetoric could be especially dangerous if used to provoke and/or justify violence.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 As a prototypical leader, Tate likely played a key role in shaping the identity of his followers (see Hogg, 2020), and, to the extent that his followers were uncertain about themselves prior to following Tate, his leadership likely provided them with a greater sense of certainty and self-esteem (see Milesi, 2022). As such, the potential loss of Tate's guidance may feel like a threat to the sense of certainty they have developed by adhering to his teachings. A lack of certainty can be psychologically uncomfortable and motivate individuals to react in antisocial ways (see Hogg, 2007, 2020).}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The future of Andrew Tate}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24
\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Banned or not, questions concerning the future of Andrew Tate, HU, and the fight against censorship are relevant. For instance, there were several references to the stages of Tate's plan, a three-phase process that promotes escaping the matrix (Dahir, 2022, para. 3). The first phase, according to Tate, is to \u8220 conquer the internet\u8221  by employing HU's affiliate program to attract more members to the site (SouljaOfLight, 2022). Then, Tate claims the second phase is a new website titled \u8220 The Real World,\u8221  a \u8220 mass portal that will allow a large-scale exodus for anyone who is still trapped inside the matrix to escape outside to enter the real world\u8221  (MotiveSuccess, 2022). Essentially, Tate envisions a platform that is not restricted by \u8220 matrix-controlled servers\u8221  and will teach the HU community to use \u8220 alternative banking systems\u8221  (Dahir, 2022, para. 50). Tate and the HU community are urging people to join Rumble and Gettr, which are free from \u8220 matrix controls\u8221  on free speech (regarding Tate on Rumble, see Sayogie et al., 2023).}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Commenters responding to Tate's final message outlined their intentions for continuing to follow his future endeavors, stating: \u8220 Stage 2..You rlly are a genius.. Crazy how you changed everything the whole internet [crying laughing emoji]\u8221 ; \u8220 Stage 2 begins guys het ready for the top g to return [fire emoji; sunglasses emoji]\u8221 ; and \u8220 Tate has been a huge inspiration in my life and i will do way beyond my best to make it, he is a genius if you understand what stage 2 and stage 3 is!\u8221  Depending on their access to the resources necessary to pay their way into the media collections associated with stage 2, some followers may be left behind in the wake of Tate's \u8220 greater purpose\u8221 \u8212 perhaps a necessary sacrifice for maintaining his male collective narcissism and position as head of the exclusive in-group; if everyone can be part of it, then no one is part of it, and he can no longer control it.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Conclusion}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The purpose of this study was to examine Andrew Tate's rhetoric and impact on social media audiences. Hegemonic masculinity and social identity frameworks gently guided our analysis as we employed a two-part analysis of \u8220 Andrew Tate Final Message,\u8221  a video posted to (and since deleted by) YouTube and the comments following his social media takedown. Our findings indicate that religious tropes are a salient theme in both Tate's farewell video as well as in the video's comments, suggesting that Tate uses male collective narcissism to present himself as a pious leader to his followers. Ultimately, we unearthed several facets of the fandom's identity, including adherence to supremacist and hegemonic narratives, and gained initial insights into why Tate's followers are drawn to his leadership style.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Although our findings are robust, a few limitations must be considered. For instance, the evolution of Hustlers University was and is particularly difficult to document due to its frequency at which it is kicked off of platforms and the number of new websites emerging in its place (i.e., HU 2.0, 3.0, The Real World, to name a few). Moreover, ambiguity surrounding the curriculum offered by HU leaves us with lingering questions about the specifics of Tate's course content. We acknowledge commenters\u8217  claims that Tate helped them in some way, but it remains unclear the }
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 exact}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2  ways in which Tate or HU helped them achieve their goals of masculinity, financial success, or improving their dating lives. We recommend future research exploring the HU curriculum more expansively along with upcoming HU platforms, new Tate content, and the evolving criminal cases involving the Tate brothers.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Despite these limitations, our study reveals that Tate's messages, while incredibly misguided and delusional to some, can point to actual long-term ramifications for his followers. For example, teacher support groups and forums are discussing how to deal with young boys who have encountered and repeated his negative assertions about women (Banting, 2022; Dimsdale, 2022; Haslop et al., 2024; Wescott et al., 2023). In the end, Andrew Tate tries to market himself as the every-man, constantly citing that he \u8220 loves women,\u8221  is actually \u8220 not a misogynist,\u8221  thinks \u8220 women are great at many things,\u8221  and that he is a \u8220 humble man\u8221  (Richards et al., 2022). Yet, his self-purported image can seem very confusing when multiple accounts of his interviews and own content promote ideals that are at complete odds with such traits.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 It is these conflicting messages that can have followers thinking they are listening to a well-balanced, nuanced message that they later repeat at others\u8217  expense without working too hard to navigate the confusion. We must take seriously the reality of an in-group that aims to radicalize men and antagonize nonbinary people and women, lest it lead to violence. We contend that Tate's rhetoric must not be dismissed as harmless online vitriol, but rather it should be taken as a sincere group effort toward establishing a new and violent \u8216 truth\u8217  for men who, though the adoption of male collective narcissism and radical in-group communication, become unwilling to face the consequences of their harmful beliefs and actions.}
